    "notes": {
      "type": "/type/text",
      "value": "\"This is Mexico is a collection of essays on the often magical and mysterious -- and sometimes heartrending -- workings of everyday life in Mexico, written from the perspective of an American expatriate. By turns humorous and poignant, Merchasin provides an informed look at Mexican culture and history, exploring everything from healthcare, Mexican-style, to religious rituals; from the educational role of the telenovela to the cultural subtleties of the Spanish language\"--Back cover.\n\nIncludes bibliographical references."
